{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1379747-a-tuatha-plot-a-campaign-idea","id":1379747,"title":"A Tuatha Plot! A Campaign Idea.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-09T06:36:10-07:00","id":1379747,"title":"A Tuatha Plot! A Campaign Idea.","content":"Since the Tuatha in the present game are depicted as hostile to the Irish it occurred to me that they might seek a weapon against the Irish people. This is an alternative history idea.<br /> <br /> Basically, soon after the events at Tilbury Camp but before the Spanish Armada's fate is known, one of the Tuatha, who has waylaid and replaced Edward Kelly, the notorious &quot;clairvoyant&quot; and con man (I'll put a link in later) contacts John Dee. The replacement Kelly then puts Dee in contact with the Tuatha.<br /> Soon Dee gives Elizabeth Tudor a cordial (healing potion) for her pains. The cordial allows the Tuatha to rejuvenate Elizabeth and restore her to the physiological conditions of her early twenties. Various well planted Tuatha use their purviews and sorcery to convince large numbers of people that God almighty blessed the cordial as a sign of favor to England.<br /> <br /> Between the defeat of the Armada and the rejuvenation of the Queen all England, Wales, and Ireland are agog. The rest of Europe ( already inclined to see Elizabeth as a little uncanny, no really) are now openly asking if she's the one who will usher in the millennial kingdom ( both Catholics and Protestants in our real history speculated about this).<br /> <br /> The Tuatha now plan to marry one of their Scions to Elizabeth. Thus grabbing the throne of England for the Tuatha through Elizabeth's children. And since England ruled Ireland in period, this would mean the Tuatha would have the whip hand in Ireland. Plus, given Elizabeth's enhanced stature in the world's eyes, shrewd dynastic marriages (aided by careful use of the Passion and Fertility purviews) would allow a dominance of Europe and easy access to the resources to kick the Irish out of Ireland.<br /> <br /> Still, achieving all that won't be easy. Most of Europe will be seeking to get Elizabeth on their side, especially the Catholic Church which will be very unhappy that God seems to be showing special favor to a Protestant. Just getting Tuatha Scions a chance to meet, let alone court, Elizabeth will be an epic challenge. Also, never underestimate Elizabeth herself. The woman was quick thinking when it suited her and could play multiple roles at once to manipulate people. Playing Elizabeth as a dupe would never be easy. And although this Elizabeth is physiologically twenty-three, she has the experience and wisdom of a fifty-six year old Elizabeth.<br /> <br /> So that's the basic idea. <br /> <br /> Comments and suggestions please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-09-2020, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:44:18-07:00","id":1380627,"title":"","content":"Hey you're allowed to comment and quibble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:03:52-07:00","id":1380686,"title":"","content":"I really love it, but I thought the Tuatha were the gods of the Irish people.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think Elizabeth was an amazing queen and I would love to see her married to (and hopefully crazy in love with) a Tuatha Scion with the Passion Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:44:16-07:00","id":1380715,"title":"","content":"The Tuatha are the gods of the Irish people. And in the 2e they don't like/ want rid of the Irish people. So, who has caused the Irish more trouble than the English, other than of course us of Irish descent ourselves? Grabbing control of England is grabbing control of the most dangerous anti-Irish weapon going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:52:12-07:00","id":1380720,"title":"","content":"Yeah, only part of Ireland is under the jurisdiction of the United Kingdom, IIRC. Elizabeth wouldn't have any legal authority of most of it.<br /> <br /> And I don't think the Tuatha would court England, because if England moved in they'd want to take over all of Ireland, and that's the TUATHA'S job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:19:54-07:00","id":1380735,"title":"","content":"Okay. But I don\u2019t understand why the gods of Ireland wouldn\u2019t like Irish people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:42:29-07:00","id":1380740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1379747-a-tuatha-plot-a-campaign-idea?p=1380735#post1380735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. But I don\u2019t understand why the gods of Ireland wouldn\u2019t like Irish people.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a fairly important part of their mythic cycle! Humanity invaded Ireland, overthrew the Pantheon, slaughtered most of them, conned their three ruling queens into betraying the Pantheon, and then forced them to live beneath the world. When the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann agreed to retreat beneath the earth on threat of 'we will finish killing you all' essentially, they left five people behind in every province of Ireland to cause as much chaos and disruption as possible. The hostilities between the humans of Ireland and the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann is a huge and important element of the stories. They really don't get on.<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann have a legal system and society that encourages blood feuds and retributive killings and that they have nothing short of an obsession with owning and controlling Ireland as established in the Book of Invasions, the hostility between the two groups is pretty justified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:06:26-07:00","id":1380747,"title":"","content":"Yeah; it's part and parcel with the way most people and their Pantheons have a \u201cwe serve our gods, and they watch over us\u201d relationship, but the Irish relationship with their Pantheon is \u201cbe very careful not to offend the Kindly Ones, because bad thing happen to those who get on the bad side of the Good Folk.\u201d On the surface, it looks the same: the people show a great deal of respect toward the Pantheon. But it's what's under the surface that differs greatly: where the typical motive for the respect is awe, with the Irish it is wariness: noble and powerful vs. dangerously powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:53:50-07:00","id":1380760,"title":"","content":"While I agree with your point, and there are more than just pointing fingers to prove the relationship between the TDD and the Irish people, I must remember that most of the population of many religions believe more by fear than by awe.<br /> <br /> I mean, most of the population in ancient Greece were afraid of the Theoi (with reason, if you paid attention in the stories), they honored the gods because if they know they would be punished if not, they would never compare themselves or any mortal to the gods or it would be a certain and horrible death for themselves and possibly the entire city, they made offers to the chtonic gods just to avoid death a little longer and when die not be treated absolutely bad (only marginally bad), as they had no chance of be treated fine. There are few stories about Hades because even the Heroes would be afraid of dealing with the one that will take care of their soul after to death.<br /> <br /> Just ask any person why they really go to church, it\u2019s to avoid going to hell. I\u2019m Portuguese you don\u2019t ask if a person believe in god (acredita em Deus), we ask if the person is \u201ctemente a Deus\u201d, what literally means afraid of god.<br /> <br /> What I mean is, while many believe their gods are the source of good things, many more just practice the gradiometers to avoid the bad side of the gods. Thats probably due to fear being a much better tool (and far easier to get) than love to the priests trying to keep people in their places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-12-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:52:20-07:00","id":1380776,"title":"","content":"Thank you. That makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T15:00:31-07:00","id":1380777,"title":"","content":"Queen Elizabeth was called Gloriana the Faerie Queene in Spenser\u2019s poem. Maybe you could have her be the agelessly beautiful ruler of a fae court that rivals the Tuatha and maybe supports anti-Tuatha sentiment among the people of Ireland. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> Thanks for clarifying about the Tuatha. I just assumed that if the Fomorians were the bad guys, the Tuatha must be the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T15:05:36-07:00","id":1380778,"title":"","content":"So,that said, how do you like the plot? <br /> <br /> How would you improve it?<br /> <br /> And how would you complicate things?<br /> <br /> Oh, and are the Tuatha ready to take on a Welsh redhead who is an anointed queen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T19:33:09-07:00","id":1380829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1379747-a-tuatha-plot-a-campaign-idea?p=1380777#post1380777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for clarifying about the Tuatha. I just assumed that if the Fomorians were the bad guys, the Tuatha must be the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, the fact that this is less clear cut is something I love. With the Tuatha and the Fomorians, it's especially a case of &quot;The God/Titan divide is basically political&quot;<br /> <br /> As for how I'd change it, well, I dunno if I'd have them try to get England involved in their land grab, unless they were playing the long con and intend on backstabbing England to declare themselves rulers of Ireland after kicking out the Milisians.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T05:42:02-07:00","id":1380921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1379747-a-tuatha-plot-a-campaign-idea?p=1380829#post1380829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a way, the fact that this is less clear cut is something I love. With the Tuatha and the Fomorians, it's especially a case of &amp;quot;The God/Titan divide is basically political&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> As for how I'd change it, well, I dunno if I'd have them try to get England involved in their land grab, unless they were playing the long con and intend on backstabbing England to declare themselves rulers of Ireland after kicking out the Milisians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less backstabbing more simply using them in a long game against Ireland. Just remember Cromwell is going to be born in a decade or two. Picture what the Tuatha could do with him. As anti-Irish weapons go, England is amazingly brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}